WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:04.420
Any movie with as troubled a production as
the new Masters of the Universe is bound to

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:07.040
foster a whole mythology of rumors and speculation.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:11.320
And by the power of Grayskull, here's all
the latest on the future adventures of Eternia's

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:12.400
greatest warrior.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:16.980
In early 2019, the final slate of production
staff for Masters of the Universe finally

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:17.880
began to gel.

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:21.720
David Goyer, who'd earlier delivered a script
treatment for the new movie and was briefly

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:26.370
in talks to direct, opted to serve as executive
producer on the project instead due to other

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:27.660
directorial commitments.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:32.400
In his place, the studio hired the directorial
sibling duo Adam and Aaron Nee, best known

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:36.720
for the comedy Band of Robbers, a modernized
pseudo-sequel take on The Adventures of Huckleberry

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.380
Finn with its main characters portrayed as
adults.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:43.720
Finally, screenwriters Art Markum and Matt
Holloway, best known for their credits on

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:46.800
the original Iron Man, have taken a fresh
pass at the script.

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:50.280
With Goyer and at least four other known writers
having made their own attempts at cracking

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:54.202
the story, it's not yet clear how much credit
any of them will receive, or if any of their

00:00:54.202 --> 00:00:56.640
previous ideas will make it into the final
product.

00:00:56.840 --> 00:01:00.640
Goyer's script in particular appeared to have
been relatively close to completion, but Markum

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:03.520
and Holloway still reportedly started over
from scratch.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:08.060
"You are all aware of the penalty for failure."

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:19.340
You can't have a Masters of the Universe movie
without a star to play He-Man, and in 2019,

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:21.980
the new version found its lead in Noah Centineo.

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:26.360
Arguably best known for his work in the Netflix
rom-com To All the Boys I've Loved Before,

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:30.720
Centineo's casting marks more than a slight
departure from his predecessor in the role,

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:31.600
Dolph Lundgren.

00:01:31.910 --> 00:01:35.820
This appears to be an intentional move, when
asked about his preparation for the project,

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:36.800
Centineo teased:

00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:41.040
"It's a new universe…The Nee brothers, Adam
and Aaron Nee, they're directing it, and they're

00:01:41.049 --> 00:01:44.590
the filmmakers in charge of the story, and
they are doing one hell of a job developing

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:45.900
the world and all these things."

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.659
A new perspective on the characters and their
setting is to be expected from any reboot

00:01:49.659 --> 00:01:53.780
of a well-known property, but, as is always
the case, fans were quick to offer their opinions

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.160
on Centineo's casting.

00:01:55.369 --> 00:01:59.340
Critical Twitter users called the young actor
everything from "a fine actor, but a poor

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:01.560
choice for He-Man" to downright "pathetic."

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:05.920
Of course, Centineo is far from the first
star to suffer the sting of preemptive scorn,

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:10.140
even Heath Ledger's initial casting as the
Joker was met with outright uproar from comic

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:10.640
fans.

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:13.620
"I thought my jokes were bad."

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:18.660
Dolph Lundgren played the original live-action
He-Man in the 1987 Masters of the Universe

00:02:18.669 --> 00:02:22.989
film, and in an era of pop culture callbacks
and novelty cameos, there's no doubt that

00:02:22.989 --> 00:02:25.519
many longtime fans would appreciate an appearance
in the reboot.

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:30.020
At one point, Lundgren was indeed actively
sought after for the movie, with previous

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:34.280
director Jon Chu having publicly expressed
an interest in including him in some way.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:38.220
This interest, however, doesn't appear to
have ever brought about any serious negotiation

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:43.240
towards casting Lundgren under Chu's direction,
and Chu departed the project in 2014.

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:46.900
Lundgren himself has in the past expressed
his own interest in being involved.

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:48.739
In 2012, he called the reboot:

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:52.000
"...a good idea…[but] I wouldn't want to
take my shirt off again for three months."

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:56.120
Lundgren then suggested that he could play
He-Man's father, King Randor, instead.

00:02:56.460 --> 00:03:00.819
Of course, that was some time ago, but Lundgren
is still very much around and enjoying a healthy

00:03:00.819 --> 00:03:05.379
bump in his celebrity status, having recently
appeared in Aquaman and having reprised his

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:07.980
famous role as Ivan Drago in Creed II.

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:12.029
Getting him involved with Masters of the Universe
would be a fun way to hark back to the franchise's

00:03:12.029 --> 00:03:14.840
history that older He-Man fans are bound to
love.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:22.300
"I have the power!"

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:26.920
When a film such as Masters of the Universe
struggles to find its feet, movie studios

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:31.170
tend to keep production updates very low-key
because of the inevitable fragility of the

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:32.290
pre-production process.

00:03:32.290 --> 00:03:35.680
As such, not much is known about how this
new film will actually look.

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:38.340
But a few choice teasers have reached fans
nonetheless.

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:42.219
The only tantalizing peeks we've yet seen
of the new movie's visual conceptualization

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:45.409
came from yet another of the movie's former
directors, Jeff Wadlow.

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:50.340
Wadlow, who was on the project from 2014 to
2017, commissioned prosthetics designer and

00:03:50.349 --> 00:03:55.249
sculptor Mario Torres to mock up some busts
of two secondary characters from Eternia:

00:03:55.249 --> 00:03:56.600
Beast-man and Ram-man.

00:03:56.790 --> 00:04:00.880
Torres later shared images of these sculptures
on his Instagram account, revealing designs

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:05.180
that seemed to indicate a more realistic and
gritty film than the 1987 original.

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:10.540
At 2019's annual Masters of the Universe fan
convention, Power-Con, director Kevin Smith

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:14.000
was announced as a last-minute Guest of Honor
just days before the con began.

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:18.139
This appearance ended up being a surprise
reveal for a brand-new animated Masters of

00:04:18.139 --> 00:04:23.139
the Universe limited series for Netflix entitled
Masters of the Universe: Revelation, with

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:25.160
Smith on board as executive producer.

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:28.960
Very little has been revealed about the project
so far, but what is known is that the story

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:33.330
is set to resolve unfinished business from
the original animated series' two seasons,

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:35.740
which ran from 1983 to 1985.

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:39.560
Currently, there is no announced release date,
but the series will be produced by the Powerhouse

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:44.080
animation studio, which was also behind Netflix's
Castlevania animated series.

00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:48.080
For the moment, there's no official word and
no reason to believe that this modern return

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:52.470
to the animated source material has anything
to do with Sony's live-action feature film.

00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:56.960
It is clear, however, that He-Man's future
is finally heating up, after a very long and

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:59.640
very cold break for longtime fans of the franchise.

